cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Attention, Explained: a step-by-step course on the attention mechanism"
message: "If you use these materials, please cite them using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hentabli
    given-names: Hamza
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9530-2815"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hentablihamza/attention-explained"
url: "https://github.com/hentablihamza/attention-explained"
abstract: >
  A hands-on, 12-notebook course that builds the attention mechanism and the Transformer
  from scratch through NLP: tokenization and embeddings, queries/keys/values, scaled
  dot-product attention worked by hand, attention heatmaps, self-attention and coreference,
  multi-head attention, positional encoding, the transformer block, causal masking, a tiny
  transformer in NumPy and PyTorch trained live, and the path to BERT and GPT. Every figure
  is generated from code executed in the notebooks; each notebook runs in Google Colab.
keywords:
  - attention
  - transformer
  - self-attention
  - natural language processing
  - deep learning
  - PyTorch
  - education
  - tutorial
date-released: "2026-11-24"
